;; stale_after_source_refresh — verified claims whose source was refreshed AFTER
;; the claim was created (REQ-KG-006).
;;
;; Booklogic port of assets/queries/coverage/stale_after_source_refresh.rq:
;;   SELECT ?claim ?claim_date ?src_date WHERE {
;;     ?claim tbf:status "verified" ;
;;            schema:dateCreated ?claim_date ;
;;            prov:wasDerivedFrom ?src .
;;     ?src schema:dateCreated ?src_date .
;;     FILTER (?src_date > ?claim_date)
;;   }
;;
;; The :where binds a verified claim's id and created_at, then joins
;; claim -> source-span (claim-id) -> source (the span's doc-id unifies with the
;; source row's id) and reads the source's ingested_at.
;;
;; DIVERGENCE FROM THE RDF QUERY — RESOLVED (P5.2): adopt this corrected doc_id
;; join as canonical. The structurally-dead RDF join is retired with project_graph
;; in P5.4; no project_graph URI-minting fix is warranted. The .rq join is in
;; fact STRUCTURALLY DEAD over the current RDF projection: project_graph mints
;; prov:wasDerivedFrom to the source-SPAN URI (.../sources/<doc>#<locator>, with a
;; fragment) while schema:dateCreated lands on the BARE manifest URI
;; (.../sources/<doc>). Those are different nodes, so `?src schema:dateCreated
;; ?src_date` never binds and the SPARQL query always returns empty (verified: all
;; 14 bermuda wasDerivedFrom targets have dateCreated = nil). This EDN port
;; implements the INTENDED semantics — join on the underlying doc_id, which
;; actually connects — so the two agree on bermuda ONLY because every claim there
;; was created at the same instant its source was ingested (equal, not strictly
;; later). On a workspace with a genuinely refreshed source the Cozo port WILL
;; fire while the broken SPARQL stays silent — which is the intended behaviour, now
;; the canonical one.
;;
;; :filter applies the var-vs-var ordered comparison `?src_date > ?claim_date`
;; (source refreshed strictly after the claim was created). Both are ISO-8601
;; strings, which Cozo compares lexically — the same total order the date compare
;; intends.
(defquery :stale-after-source-refresh
  :find   [?claim ?claim-date ?src-date]
  :where  [[?c :claim/id ?claim]
           [?c :claim/status "verified"]
           [?c :claim/created-at ?claim-date]
           [?span :source-span/claim-id ?claim]
           [?span :source-span/doc-id ?src]
           [?s :source/id ?src]
           [?s :source/ingested-at ?src-date]]
  :filter [[> ?src-date ?claim-date]])
